      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shrinker\u0027s count_objects (freelist_shrink_count) and scan_objects (free_one_item) return the number of pages. So looks like you consider pages as freeable items of your cache. However the way cache size (list_size_pages) is calculated is via incrementing/decrementing by (size \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT). If \"size\" is less that PAGE_SIZE then the accounting will be broken. You can end up with multi-page aggregate cache which reports 0 shrinkable items. If expectation is that \"size\" is always a multiple of PAGE_SIZE then IMHO it\u0027s better to use number of pages instead of number of bytes for deferred_freelist_item.size.",
      "parentUuid": "d35e3e7f_9d5f893c",
